+Tile01 contains no additive raster over roughly the top 23% and right 25% of the
+scan.  The existing border/known-range logic correctly treats that as a partial
+screen: with the 2 / 3 mask it analyzes 56.04% of the whole image but 97.33% of
+the actual screen area.  Tile05 is an interior control and shows the remaining
+problem clearly: even after DG-024, removing the old mask still reduces flood
+fill coverage to 86.67%.  That points to DG-009/class-map continuity as the next
+robustness problem rather than to a wider seed-neighborhood search.
 
